ile doesn't exist, so it exits 1 before node starts (`bash: samples-dir: No such file or directory`). Separately, `.theseus/oracle/perf/profile-fonts.js` is not on this branch. The command fails before it touches the code, so fixing `StringRender.js` cannot make it pass. PKT-0080 was blocked by the same failure, and PKT-0083 (pending) already exists to fix the placeholder.\n\n**The code change is unchanged from the last attempt** (sdkjs clone, commit `f11c1d1`): a size-limited cache in `StringRender.js` keyed by font, size, bold/italic, PPI and text. When a cell's text and font haven't changed, the shaped result is reused instead of going back to HarfBuzz (`HB_ShapeText`). The cached data is what the shaper writes on a fresh call, so widths, wrapping and bidi should be unchanged. It has only been syntax-checked: I have not built it or profiled it, so the drop in shaping calls and font time hasn't been measured.\n\n**What I did this attempt:**\n- Added an entry to the Executor log saying why it still fails and what the factory needs to do.\n- Appended a friction line saying the factory should not re-send a packet whose acceptance command fails with a shell error.\n- `theseus validate` reported 0 errors and 1 warning (the warning text wasn't captured).\n- Committed as `9230107`.\n\n**Needed from the factory:** fix the acceptance line (point it at a real samples directory and make `profile-fonts.js` available). Then add `depends_on: [PKT-0083]` to this packet and re-run it. Another retry with the same command will fail the same way and use up the last attempt.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- Spreadsheet (xlsx) remote apply is slow because of how many times text gets shaped, not the cost of each shaping. Caching shaped text by (font, PPI, text) cuts out the repeats.\n- Packets with `<…>` placeholders in their acceptance commands shouldn't be queued.","ttft_ms":1784,"type":"result","duration_ms":21184,"uuid":"2dfe880c-eae4-49c7-9847-0b275e519cb2","ttft_stream_ms":864,"t